1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,652
Last time your boss was a copy of the Warlord with new names.

2
00:00:06,552 --> 00:00:10,465
So she flew a Kralien dreadnought, with Kralien escorts,

3
00:00:10,915 --> 00:00:12,654
and a corsair shouldn't.

4
00:00:14,454 --> 00:00:18,367
Today you change six lines, one at a time,

5
00:00:18,817 --> 00:00:24,470
and by the end, every number in her file is one you chose.

6
00:00:25,670 --> 00:00:28,713
Everything today is in the first fence.

7
00:00:29,613 --> 00:00:33,091
Trigger says which kind of boss she is.

8
00:00:33,541 --> 00:00:35,715
Low says when she arrives.

9
00:00:36,615 --> 00:00:40,528
Fleets, Flies and Difficulty say what comes with her,

10
00:00:40,978 --> 00:00:44,457
and Named says which ships carry a name.

11
00:00:46,257 --> 00:00:48,430
One thing before we start.

12
00:00:49,330 --> 00:00:53,678
The game reads a boss file when the mission starts,

13
00:00:54,128 --> 00:00:56,737
so after every change you save,

14
00:00:57,187 --> 00:00:59,361
you start the mission again.

15
00:01:00,561 --> 00:01:04,039
You're going to play her several times today,

16
00:01:04,489 --> 00:01:09,272
and you don't want to fight for ten minutes each time.

17
00:01:10,172 --> 00:01:13,215
So set Low to a hundred percent.

18
00:01:14,115 --> 00:01:17,159
Low is a share of the raiders,

19
00:01:17,609 --> 00:01:21,957
and she comes when that share or less is left.

20
00:01:23,757 --> 00:01:29,843
A hundred percent is all of them, so she arrives about four seconds in,

21
00:01:30,293 --> 00:01:32,902
before anyone has fired a shot.

22
00:01:33,802 --> 00:01:35,541
That's your test setting,

23
00:01:35,991 --> 00:01:40,339
and you put the real number back at the end.

24
00:01:41,539 --> 00:01:47,191
Fleets is the easy one. It's a whole number, written as a digit,

25
00:01:47,641 --> 00:01:51,120
and that many escort fleets arrive with her.

26
00:01:52,020 --> 00:01:53,759
Flies names a race,

27
00:01:54,209 --> 00:01:58,122
and there are six that can fly a fleet.

28
00:01:59,922 --> 00:02:02,965
Now here's the part people get wrong.

29
00:02:03,865 --> 00:02:07,343
Seventy-five percent pirate, twenty-five Kralien, with three fleets,

30
00:02:07,793 --> 00:02:11,707
doesn't give you two pirate fleets and one Kralien.

31
00:02:12,607 --> 00:02:15,650
The game rolls once, when she arrives,

32
00:02:16,100 --> 00:02:19,578
and all three fleets are the same race.

33
00:02:20,478 --> 00:02:23,522
So write the mix as a story:

34
00:02:23,972 --> 00:02:27,015
most nights she brings her own corsairs,

35
00:02:27,465 --> 00:02:30,509
and now and then she's hired Kraliens.

36
00:02:31,709 --> 00:02:36,926
The crew picks a difficulty before the game, from one to eleven.

37
00:02:37,826 --> 00:02:42,609
Your line says how hard her fleets are next to that.

38
00:02:43,509 --> 00:02:46,987
Plus two is two levels above the game,

39
00:02:47,437 --> 00:02:52,654
so in a game at five, her fleets are built for seven.

40
00:02:54,454 --> 00:02:59,237
And the level decides how many ships are in a fleet.

41
00:03:00,137 --> 00:03:04,485
At seven, a pirate fleet is one to three ships,

42
00:03:04,935 --> 00:03:08,413
and a Kralien fleet is four to six.

43
00:03:09,313 --> 00:03:13,661
So the night she's hired Kraliens is the hard night.

44
00:03:14,861 --> 00:03:17,904
Named is two words for each ship:

45
00:03:18,354 --> 00:03:21,833
its name, and then which ship it is.

46
00:03:22,733 --> 00:03:25,776
Last time you changed the first word.

47
00:03:26,226 --> 00:03:28,400
Today you change the second,

48
00:03:28,850 --> 00:03:32,763
and you add a second ship after a comma.

49
00:03:34,563 --> 00:03:37,607
The second word is a ship key,

50
00:03:38,057 --> 00:03:42,404
and the page has the raider ships in a table.

51
00:03:43,304 --> 00:03:48,522
Type it exactly as it's printed, in small letters, with the underscores,

52
00:03:48,972 --> 00:03:54,624
because this is the one line where a spelling mistake gets past everything.

53
00:03:55,824 --> 00:03:59,302
Lint reads the shape of a boss line.

54
00:04:00,202 --> 00:04:02,376
It knows the field names,

55
00:04:02,826 --> 00:04:05,000
it knows the two triggers,

56
00:04:05,450 --> 00:04:09,363
and it knows a named ship is two words.

57
00:04:11,163 --> 00:04:13,772
It doesn't check the other values.

58
00:04:14,672 --> 00:04:19,889
So if I write pirates, with an S, lint still says clean,

59
00:04:20,339 --> 00:04:25,991
and in the game her named ships arrive with no fleets at all.

60
00:04:26,891 --> 00:04:29,500
The game does tell you, though.

61
00:04:29,950 --> 00:04:35,602
It writes one line in the runtime log, in the Legendary Missions folder,

62
00:04:36,052 --> 00:04:38,661
naming the race it couldn't find.

63
00:04:39,561 --> 00:04:42,604
And for a number it can't read,

64
00:04:43,054 --> 00:04:48,272
it leaves your boss out of the list and says which line.

65
00:04:49,472 --> 00:04:52,515
Now play it, and count what arrives.

66
00:04:53,415 --> 00:04:56,893
Two named ships, the Morrigan and the Badb.

67
00:04:57,343 --> 00:05:00,387
Three new fleets, all of one race.

68
00:05:01,287 --> 00:05:05,635
Then start the mission again and look a second time,

69
00:05:06,085 --> 00:05:10,433
because about one arrival in four is the Kralien one.

70
00:05:12,233 --> 00:05:15,276
Try changing one number and playing again.

71
00:05:16,176 --> 00:05:18,785
Set the difficulty line to eleven,

72
00:05:19,235 --> 00:05:21,843
and every fleet is six ships.

73
00:05:23,043 --> 00:05:28,696
Testing's over, so give her the number you want the crew to play.

74
00:05:29,596 --> 00:05:31,335
I'm using forty percent.

75
00:05:32,235 --> 00:05:34,843
With sixteen raiders at the start,

76
00:05:35,293 --> 00:05:37,902
she comes when six are left.

77
00:05:38,802 --> 00:05:40,976
The crew's winning by then,

78
00:05:41,426 --> 00:05:43,600
but the siege isn't over.

79
00:05:45,400 --> 00:05:51,052
Then bring the note at the top of the file up to date.

80
00:05:51,952 --> 00:05:54,996
It's for you, a year from now,

81
00:05:55,446 --> 00:05:59,359
when you've forgotten why she flies what she flies.

82
00:06:00,259 --> 00:06:03,737
Next time she gets objectives of her own.
